  "raw_label": "1",
  "texts": {
    "preamble": "Satya Pal S/O Late Pralad Raj vs D.V.Singh on 25 October, 2018 In The Court Of Ms. Poonam A. Bamba District & Sessions Judge, New Delhi In the matters of : Fsat No. 40/2016 1. Satya Pal S/o Late Pralad Raj M/s Adarsh Suppliers Company 2/26 Roop Nagar, Delhi110007. 2. Sunil Aggarwal S/o Late Sudesh Pal M / s Adarsh Suppliers Company 2/26 Roop Nagar, Delhi110007. 3. M / s Adarsh Suppliers Company Through its Authorized Representative Sunil Aggarwal .....Appellants Versus D.V.Singh Food Safety Officer Department of Food Safety Govt. of Nct of Delhi. ..... Respondent Appeal Against The Order Dated 18.03.2016 Of Ld. Adjudicating Officer/ Adm, (North District), Delhi. Fsat No. 40/16 Satya Pal & Ors. vs Food Safety Officer Date of filing of appeal Arguments concluded on Date of judgment J U D G M E N T :",
    "facts": "1.0 Vide this appeal, the appellants have challenged order dated 18.03.2016 (\"the impugned order\" in short) passed by Ld. Adjudicating Officer/Additional District Magistrate (North District) (\"ADM\" in short), directing Sh.Rajender Kumar S/o Late Bansi Lal, M/s Madan Store, A1, Gujrawalan Town, Delhi110009 to pay penalty of Rs.50,000/ and the above appellants namely Sh.Satya Pal, Sh.Sunil Aggarwal,partners M/s Adarsh Suppliers Company and the firm to pay penalty of Rs.1,50,000/, under Section 52 of the Food Safety and Standard Act, 2006 (\"FSS Act\" Satya Pal S/O Late Pralad Raj vs D.V.Singh on 25 October, 2018 Indian Kanoon - http://indiankanoon.org/doc/175722834/ 1 in short) for violation of Regulation 2.2.2.10 of The Food Safety & Standards (Packaging & Labeling) Regulations, 2011 (\"FSS (P&L) Regulations\" in short). 2.0 Briefly stating the facts relevant for disposal appeal are that: (i) on 9th July, 2015, Food Safety Officer (\"FSO\" in short), purchased 4 sealed packets of \"Haldi Powder\" FSAT No. 40/16 Satya Pal & Ors. vs Food Safety Officer from Sh.Rajender Kumar, s/o Late Sh.Bansi Lal of M/s Madan Store, A1 Gujranwala Town, Delhi 110009(Food Business Operator)(FBO), where the said food article was found stored for sale for h consumption. One counterpart of the sample under sealed cover was sent to Food Analyst on 10.07.2015. Other two counterparts of the sample were depo with Designated Officer. As the FBO did not request to send the fourth counter part for analysis from NABL accredited laboratory, the fourth sealed counterpart was also deposited with the Designated Officer ; (ii) the Food Analyst vide his report dated 22.07.2015 opined \" The sample is misbranded because there is violation of Regulation 2.2.2.10 of FSS (P&L) Regulations\"; (iii) the Food Safety Officer, filed a complaint/application under Rule 3.1.1(3) FSS Rule,2011 before Ld. ADM alleging violation of Section 26 2(ii) FSS Act for violation of Reg 2.2.2.10 of FSS(P&L) Regulations, punishable u/S 52 of FSAT No. 40/16 Satya Pal & Ors. vs Food Safety Officer FSS Act. Notices of the same were issued to appellants and hearing was given; (iv) during the course of hearing, Sh.Rajender Kumar,FBO on 26.11.2015 admitted the mistake. The appellants herein filed reply raising various contentions. 3.0 The appellants have challenged the impugned order on the following grounds: (i) the Ld.ADM did not appreciate that there w Satya Pal S/O Late Pralad Raj vs D.V.Singh on 25 October, 2018 Indian Kanoon - http://indiankanoon.org/doc/175722834/ 2 evidence on record against the appellant no.1 2/partners of appellant no.3 that they were incharge and responsible for day to day business of the f therefore, they could not have been prosecuted/penalised simply for being partners; (ii) Ld.ADM did not even appreciate that there was no evidence on record to demonstrate that the sample food FSAT No. 40/16 Satya Pal & Ors. vs Food Safety Officer article/Haldi Powder was not sold by the appellant no.3 firm to the vendor/FSO Sh.Rajender Kumar. The appellant no.3 does not have any business dealings with the shop or the owner of M/s Madan Store;",
    "arguments": "4.0 On the other hand, Ld. Chief Public Prosecutor for the State submitted that this appeal is not maintainable as the appellants pleaded guilty before the Ld. Trial Court.",
    "petitioner_arguments": "4.0 On the other hand, Ld. Chief Public Prosecutor for the State submitted that this appeal is not maintainable as the appellants pleaded guilty before the Ld. Trial Court.",
    "respondent_arguments": "",
    "other_lawyer_arguments": ""
  },
